index 0000000..ecb5d72
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/ops/logging-and-alerts.md
@@ -0,0 +1,82 @@
+# Observability: archive / audit / alert
+
+Three lanes. Pick exactly one per event.
+
+| Lane | Mechanism | Destination | When to use |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| **Archive** | `Log::debug/info/warning/error(...)` (default `stack` → `daily`) | `storage/logs/laravel.log` (rotated daily, 14 days) | Routine application logs: request flow, job progress, caught-and-handled errors, debug context. Noisy is fine. Nobody is paged. |
+| **Audit** | `Log::channel('audit')->info(...)` | `storage/logs/audit.log` (rotated daily, 90 days, min level `info`) | Durable "who changed / tried what" trail: membership role changes, subscription transitions, login lockouts, admin actions, permission denials. Keep entries structured (`['actor_id' => ..., 'entity_id' => ...]`) and never log secrets. |
+| **Alert** | `App\Ops\DiscordOpsAlert::send($title, $message, $context)` | Discord incoming webhook (`DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL`) | Human-pageable ops incidents only: a job that exhausted retries, a payment-gateway webhook failing, a plan limit blocking an entity. Code explicitly decides the incident is worth waking someone up for. |
+
+## Decision guide
+
+1. Is a human expected to act **now** (production incident)?
+   → **Alert** via `DiscordOpsAlert`. Keep the title short, put the
+   actionable detail in the message, add identifiers (`entity_id`,
+   `queue`, `job`) as context. Do **not** add routine info here.
+2. Is it a record of who did / tried what that we may need weeks later
+   (support, security review, billing dispute)?
+   → **Audit** via `Log::channel('audit')`. Minimum level `info`;
+   `debug` writes are dropped.
+3. Everything else → **Archive** via the default logger.
+
+Rules:
+
+- Discord is **never** a Monolog log channel. There is intentionally no
+  `discord` channel in `config/logging.php`. Alerts are explicit
+  `DiscordOpsAlert::send()` calls, not log routing.
+- The notifier soft-fails: transport errors and non-2xx responses are
+  logged at `error` level and never throw. The webhook URL (it embeds the
+  token) is never written to logs.
+- Alert context is redacted before sending: sensitive keys (`password`,
+  `token`, `secret`, `authorization`, `api_key`/`api-key`/`apikey`,
+  `webhook`, case-insensitive) become `[redacted]`; any value containing
+  `Bearer <...>` becomes `[redacted]`; nested arrays are redacted
+  recursively and rendered as JSON. Payloads are truncated to 1800 chars.
+- Do not wire the notifier into every exception handler or noisy path.
+  Out of scope by design: embeds, mentions, rate limiting, retries,
+  external log shipping.
+
+## Configuration
+
+```dotenv
+LOG_CHANNEL=stack
+LOG_STACK=daily
+LOG_LEVEL=debug
+LOG_DAILY_DAYS=14
+LOG_AUDIT_LEVEL=info
+LOG_AUDIT_DAYS=90
+DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL=
+```
+
+- `LOG_STACK`: channels behind the `stack` channel (default `daily`).
+- `LOG_DAILY_DAYS` (default `14`): retention for the archive (`daily`) channel.
+- `LOG_AUDIT_LEVEL` (default `info`): minimum level for the `audit` channel.
+- `LOG_AUDIT_DAYS` (default `90`): retention for the `audit` channel.
+- `DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL` (default empty): Discord incoming webhook.
+  Empty/unset = alerts are a silent no-op (useful for local/test).
+
+Examples:
+
+```php
+use App\Ops\DiscordOpsAlert;
+use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Log;
+
+// Archive: routine log.
+Log::info('Asaas webhook received', ['queue' => 'asaas-webhooks']);
+
+// Audit: durable trail.
+Log::channel('audit')->info('Subscription status changed', [
+    'actor_id' => $user->id,
+    'subscription_id' => $subscription->id,
+    'from' => 'trialing',
+    'to' => 'past_due',
+]);
+
+// Alert: page ops (explicit, rare).
+app(DiscordOpsAlert::class)->send(
+    'Asaas webhooks failing',
+    '5 failures in 10 minutes on queue asaas-webhooks.',
+    ['queue' => 'asaas-webhooks', 'entity_id' => 42],
+);
+```
